---
description: Use switch/getUnreachableError for discriminated union exhaustion, not if/continue or if/return.
globs: '**/*.ts,**/*.tsx'
alwaysApply: true
---

When branching on a discriminated union's `.type` property (e.g., `output.type`), use a `switch` statement with `getUnreachableError` in the `default` case. This ensures exhaustiveness — adding a new union member causes a compile error at the `default` branch rather than silently falling through.

## Examples

```ts
// Avoid — adding a new union member silently falls through
for (const output of Object.values(outputs)) {
  if (output.type !== 'form') continue;
  // process form output
}
```

```ts
// Avoid — adding a new union member silently returns
for (const output of Object.values(outputs)) {
  if (output.type === 'form') {
    // process form output
    continue;
  }
  if (output.type === 'evidence') {
    // process evidence output
    continue;
  }
  // missing default!
}
```

```ts
// Prefer — adding a new union member causes a TypeScript error
import { getUnreachableError } from 'lib/typescript/getUnreachableError';

for (const output of Object.values(outputs)) {
  switch (output.type) {
    case 'form': {
      // process form output
      break;
    }
    case 'evidence': {
      // process evidence output
      break;
    }
    default:
      throw getUnreachableError(output);
  }
}
```

```ts
// Also OK — if/else if/else with getUnreachableError for non-throwing paths
function process(output: FormSetPDFOutput): Result | null {
  if (output.type === 'form') {
    return processForm(output);
  } else if (output.type === 'evidence') {
    return processEvidence(output);
  } else {
    // Exhaustive: all variants handled above
    getUnreachableError(output);
    return null; // unreachable but satisfies TypeScript
  }
}
```

## Exceptions

- Early returns/continues are acceptable when the function is genuinely
  handling only a subset of variants and making that choice explicitly
  (e.g., a helper that only processes form-type outputs). In that case,
  document the intentional subset in a comment.
